{"id":"2258152dd7a3f9d8","group":"27","path":"27/27-thm-gurvich.md","title":"Gurvich characterization of positive read-once functions","display":"thm-gurvich — Gurvich characterization of positive read-once functions","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Boolean Functions: Theory, Algorithms, and Applications","book_abbrev":"27","label":"27-thm-gurvich","aliases":["27-thm-gurvich"],"display":"thm-gurvich — Gurvich characterization of positive read-once functions","depends_on":["[[27-df-minmaxsupport]]","[[27-df-readoncefunc]]","[[27-thm-readoncepositive]]"],"source_file":"C:\\Users\\lzy\\Documents\\BaiduSyncdisk\\calibre\\Yves Crama, Peter L. Hammer\\Boolean Functions_ Theory, Algorith (5073)\\Boolean Functions_ Theory, Algo - Yves Crama, Peter L. Hammer.pdf","source_section":"§10.3 Theorem 10.6(i),(iv)","source_printed_pages":"458–463","source_pdf_pages":"482–487","verification_status":"source-statement-checked-full-proof-not-independently-reverified"},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Boolean Functions: Theory, Algorithms, and Applications"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"27"},{"key":"label","html":"27-thm-gurvich"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>27-thm-gurvich</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"thm-gurvich — Gurvich characterization of positive read-once functions"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"a38b86e606184c7f\" href=\"?note=a38b86e606184c7f\" title=\"27-df-minmaxsupport\">27-df-minmaxsupport</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"abdabeb50455fed9\" href=\"?note=abdabeb50455fed9\" title=\"27-df-readoncefunc\">27-df-readoncefunc</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"f98fb2ec31a9f521\" href=\"?note=f98fb2ec31a9f521\" title=\"27-thm-readoncepositive\">27-thm-readoncepositive</a></span></div>"},{"key":"source_file","html":"C:\\Users\\lzy\\Documents\\BaiduSyncdisk\\calibre\\Yves Crama, Peter L. Hammer\\Boolean Functions_ Theory, Algorith (5073)\\Boolean Functions_ Theory, Algo - Yves Crama, Peter L. Hammer.pdf"},{"key":"source_section","html":"§10.3 Theorem 10.6(i),(iv)"},{"key":"source_printed_pages","html":"458–463"},{"key":"source_pdf_pages","html":"482–487"},{"key":"verification_status","html":"source-statement-checked-full-proof-not-independently-reverified"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"n\\in\\mathbb N\">\\(n\\in\\mathbb N\\)</span>，<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"f\\in\\mathrm{Monotone}_n\">\\(f\\in\\mathrm{Monotone}_n\\)</span>；<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathcal M(f),\\mathcal X(f)\">\\(\\mathcal M(f),\\mathcal X(f)\\)</span> 见 <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"a38b86e606184c7f\" href=\"?note=a38b86e606184c7f\" title=\"27-df-minmaxsupport\">27-df-minmaxsupport</a>。</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ReadOnceFunc}_n,\\mathrm{PosReadOnceFunc}_n\">\\(\\mathrm{ReadOnceFunc}_n,\\mathrm{PosReadOnceFunc}_n\\)</span> 见 <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"abdabeb50455fed9\" href=\"?note=abdabeb50455fed9\" title=\"27-df-readoncefunc\">27-df-readoncefunc</a>，其正部分接口见 <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-6\" data-note=\"f98fb2ec31a9f521\" href=\"?note=f98fb2ec31a9f521\" title=\"27-thm-readoncepositive\">27-thm-readoncepositive</a>。</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\left(f\\in\\mathrm{PosReadOnceFunc}_n\\ \\Longleftrightarrow\\ f\\in\\mathrm{ReadOnceFunc}_n\\right)\\land\\left(f\\in\\mathrm{ReadOnceFunc}_n\\ \\Longleftrightarrow\\ \\forall A\\in\\mathcal M(f)\\;\\forall B\\in\\mathcal X(f)\\;(|A\\cap B|=1)\\right).\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\left(f\\in\\mathrm{PosReadOnceFunc}_n\\ \\Longleftrightarrow\\ f\\in\\mathrm{ReadOnceFunc}_n\\right)\\land\\left(f\\in\\mathrm{ReadOnceFunc}_n\\ \\Longleftrightarrow\\ \\forall A\\in\\mathcal M(f)\\;\\forall B\\in\\mathcal X(f)\\;(|A\\cap B|=1)\\right).\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>原书 §10.3，Theorem 10.6(i),(iv)，印刷 p.458／PDF p.482；已逐项核对正性假设与陈述。原书证明位于印刷 pp.458–463／PDF pp.482–487；本次读取了首尾与主要构造页，但未逐行复验整个多页证明，故只主张来源陈述对应。</li>\n<li>将三项等价写成两个双条件的合取，避免将连续二元双条件解释成迭代真值运算；数学结论不变。</li>\n<li>原书用 prime implicants of <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"f\">\\(f\\)</span> 与 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"f^d\">\\(f^d\\)</span>；对正函数，它们对应本目录 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathcal M(f),\\mathcal X(f)\">\\(\\mathcal M(f),\\mathcal X(f)\\)</span>。显式正性不能从题名或 Remark 才补入。</li>\n<li>常 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"0\">\\(0\\)</span> 或常 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"1\">\\(1\\)</span> 时一个量词域为空，右端为真；两者都有常量 read-once 表示，与本目录的扩展约定一致。带虚变量时两个支持族均不包含虚变量，故删去虚变量后可应用书中本质变量版本，再把所得表达式视作 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"n\">\\(n\\)</span> 变量表达式。</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"27-df-minmaxsupport","status":"resolved","id":"a38b86e606184c7f","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[27-df-minmaxsupport]]","embed":false},{"target":"27-df-readoncefunc","status":"resolved","id":"abdabeb50455fed9","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[27-df-readoncefunc]]","embed":false},{"target":"27-thm-readoncepositive","status":"resolved","id":"f98fb2ec31a9f521","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[27-thm-readoncepositive]]","embed":false},{"target":"27-df-minmaxsupport","status":"resolved","id":"a38b86e606184c7f","anchor":"ref-4","targ